$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a 500 mL two-neck flask, 3,4-dibromoaniline (4.52 g, 18.0 mmol),
2-(5-hexylthiophen-2-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (12.70
g, 43.2 mmol), tetrabutylammonium bromide (TBAB, 3.0 g, 9.32 mmol), 100
mL toluene and 100 mL Na2CO3 aqueous solution (2 M) were added. The
mixture was degassed by three times of freeze-pump-thaw operation, and
then Pd(PPh3)4 (420 mg, 0.36 mmol) was added. The mixture was refluxed
for 4 h, cooled to room temperature, and poured into 200 mL water. After
an extraction with 100 mL ethyl acetate, the solvent of the organic phase
was removed under vacuum and the resulting residue was purified by silica
gel column chromatography. The target compound as colorless oil (7.05 g,
92%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ = 7.08 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H),
6.66-6.61 (m, 4H), 6.56-6.54 (m, 2H), 5.36 (s, 2H), 2.71 (t, J = 7.5 Hz,
2H), 2.68 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 1.58-1.50 (m, 4H), 1.31-1.23 (m, 12H),
0.87-0.84 (m, 6H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 145.24, 144.72, 144.50,
139.62, 139.21, 133.90, 130.98, 125.37, 124.77, 123.34, 122.76, 122.61,
115.85, 113.13, 30.62, 30.61, 30.56, 29.09, 29.06, 27.71, 21.58, 13.08.
MS m/z: 425.22 [M]+ (calcd: 425.22).
