$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure G: Suzuki-Miyaura coupling. A solution of heteroaryl
halide (1.0 equiv), aryl boronic acid (1.0 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (2.5 mol%),
and Cs2CO3 (2.5 equiv) in 2:1 EtOH/H2O (1.0 M) was stirred at 80 °C.
After cooling to 23 °C, H2O was added. The aqueous phase was extracted
with EtOAc (3x). The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure. The
crude material was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexanes/EtOAc). 2-(2-Methoxyphenyl)pyrazine (S18): Prepared by the
general procedure G from iodopyrazine (1.00 g, 4.85 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
2-methoxyphenyl boronic acid (737 mg, 4.85 mmol, 1.0 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4
(140 mg, 12.1 μmol, 2.5 mol%) and Cs2CO3 (3.95 g, 12.1 mmol, 2.5 equiv),
purified by column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc) and isolated as a
yellow oil (831 mg, 92% yield). Spectroscopic data matched those
reported.38
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of chemically and configurationally stable monofluoro
acylboronates: effect of ligand structure on their formation, properties,
and reactivities
